<title>JAPAN: TOSHOKU ASK-ONLY ON LOAN CANCELLATION.</title>
<headline>TOSHOKU ASK-ONLY ON LOAN CANCELLATION.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Japanese foodstuffs trader Toshoku Ltd were ask-only on Monday morning on the news announced on Friday that it would forgive 49.41 billion yen worth of loans to its wholly owned finance unit.</p>
<p>At 0109 GMT, Toshoku's shares were ask-only at 205 yen against Friday's 230 yen.</p>
<p>Toshoku said on Friday that it had decided to forgive its loans to the unit as part of a restructuring of the unit's business.</p>
</text>
